COLUMNS
int ID
float Pos // a polygon corner in yards, (game X, game Y): proven from the bytes (the polygons named after cities hold those cities' TaxiNodes; read as (Y, X) they would not)
int PointOrder // the corner's place in its polygon, 1 to n with no gap: proven from the bytes (every polygon of Retail, PTR, Classic Beta and MoP Classic)
int ZoneLightID // the ZoneLight row the corner belongs to, from the section's relationship map: proven from the bytes (every readable ZoneLight row has its points; Classic Beta has one group of 4 whose ZoneLight row it cannot decrypt)

COMMENT Written for WoW Model Viewer's light catalogue (wow::LightCatalog: the zone light's water colours,
COMMENT docs/world-viewer/09-liquids.md). The layout comes from public table definitions, read as hypotheses: every column
COMMENT was checked against the clients' own bytes. Its hash is the same in Retail 12.1.5, PTR 12.1.7, Classic Beta 1.60.1,
COMMENT Classic Era 1.15.9 and MoP Classic 5.5.4; Classic Era's table has no rows (and no section). A layout not listed here
COMMENT is not read.

